SDK patch 0309 (Max Payne 3 port): x360_resolve_exp_previsto. A resolve with an exp bias is written already scaled by
the exp_adjust the texture's last fetch used (exp_previo), and a fetch with that exp_adjust samples it directly; any
other one scales only the rest. Max Payne 3 resolved its HDR scene x2048 and every read (exp_adjust -13) made another
full 960x540 RGBA16F copy x1/8192: about 0.5 ms each on the GPU. Resolves read back to guest memory, shrunk with a
blit or presented lazily keep no extra scale.

--- a/include/rex/x360/deko/render.h
+++ b/include/rex/x360/deko/render.h
@@ -90,6 +90,11 @@
   // A 7e3 target resolved into k_16_16_16_16 or k_16_16: it holds the 16-bit integers (v x 2^copy exp bias), which a
   // fetch as a fraction divides by 65535 (texturas.cpp).
   bool entero16 = false;
+  // x360_resolve_exp_previsto: the power of two the resolve already applied beyond its exp bias (the exp_adjust the
+  // last fetch of this texture used), so a fetch with that exp_adjust samples it directly instead of a scaled copy.
+  int8_t exp_previo = 0;
+  mutable int8_t exp_leida = 0;
+  mutable bool exp_leida_valida = false;
   uint64_t serie = 0;  // unique per creation: the key of its descriptors
   uint64_t version = 0;  // resolved textures: goes up every time a resolve writes it (the cubemaps' faces)
   // Render targets only, and they stay with the target when its image is swapped (IntercambiarImagenes):
